2900:## 2026-10-25 - US-056
2901-- What was implemented: the script lifecycle in `engine_script`. `ScriptRunner` (`script_runner.hpp/.cpp`) attaches a chunk to an entity and calls `create`, `start`, `fixed_update`, `update`, and `destroy` in the documented order (`begin_frame` runs create/start for pending instances and drops dead entities; `fixed_update` then `update` each frame; `detach`/`stop_all` run destroy). Each instance has its own environment. A raised error faults only that instance and is queued on the engine console queue. `reload` keeps the old state with `ReloadPolicy::PreserveExports` (`export_state`/`import_state`) or starts fresh with `ResetState`. A syntax error on reload changes nothing. Event subscriptions carry an owner tag, released with the instance.
